      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Breeze%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1922 and 1951, Black entrepreneurs opened Seabreeze and Freeman Beaches, the first Black beach resorts on North Carolina’s coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dncr.nc.gov/blog/2023/12/12/seabreeze-and-freeman-beaches-d-124",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Freeman family, prominent landowners since 1850, supplied the acreage that became these historic resorts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dncr.nc.gov/blog/2023/12/12/seabreeze-and-freeman-beaches-d-124",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the Jim Crow era, Seabreeze and Freeman Beaches offered a rare, welcoming escape for Black vacationers from across the South.",
